Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC] drm/imagination: Hold the Cubie A7A GPU PLL during active periods

The A733 GPU node names the dedicated GPU PLL "clk_parent" even when its
core mux selects a peripheral PLL. Take one reference to this clock before
enabling the core in resume. Match that reference on suspend and unwind.
A rebind which inherits an already active device acquires the reference at
probe before the first register access.

Target: powervr-eval-source 37c3dc14 plus 0008 (baseline e71a37c3).

--- a/pvr_device.c
+++ b/pvr_device.c
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@
 	pvr_dev->sys_clk = sys_clk;
 	pvr_dev->mem_clk = mem_clk;
 
-	return 0;
+	return pvr_power_init_a733_parent(pvr_dev);
 }
 
 static int pvr_device_reset_init(struct pvr_device *pvr_dev)
@@ -650,6 +650,11 @@
 	err = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(dev);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
+
+	/* Rebinding can inherit an active device without a resume callback. */
+	err = pvr_power_hold_a733_parent(pvr_dev);
+	if (err)
+		goto err_pm_runtime_put;
 
 	/* Map the control registers into memory. */
 	err = pvr_device_reg_init(pvr_dev);

